message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” element rotating around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card on Hover</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up a 3‑D context for the whole page */
body {
    margin: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    background: #f0f0f0;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the rotation */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card container – keeps the front & back together */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3‑D children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  The front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide the reverse side while rotating */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* 4️⃣  Front styling */
.card .front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* 5️⃣  Back styling – rotated 180° so it’s hidden initially */
.card .back {
    background: #4a90e2;
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Start hidden */
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
}

/* 6️⃣  Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `<body>` | Gives depth to the 3‑D rotation. |
| 2 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face during rotation. |
| 4–5 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Positions the back face behind the front. |
| 6 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card, revealing the back. |

You can replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other content you like. Adjust the `width`, `height`, `border-radius`, and colors to fit your design. Enjoy!
